1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:01,938
In November 1923,

2
00:00:01,938 --> 00:00:03,192
a single loaf of bread in

3
00:00:03,192 --> 00:00:05,918
Berlin cost two hundred billion marks.

4
00:00:06,059 --> 00:00:07,093
Ten years earlier,

5
00:00:07,093 --> 00:00:08,658
it cost less than one.

6
00:00:08,869 --> 00:00:11,226
Germany owed huge war reparations,

7
00:00:11,226 --> 00:00:12,526
so the government did the easy

8
00:00:12,526 --> 00:00:13,291
thing.

9
00:00:13,501 --> 00:00:14,697
It printed money.

10
00:00:14,697 --> 00:00:16,936
Prices doubled every few days.

11
00:00:17,019 --> 00:00:18,679
Workers were paid twice a day

12
00:00:18,679 --> 00:00:19,945
and ran to spend it before

13
00:00:19,945 --> 00:00:21,162
it lost value.

14
00:00:21,303 --> 00:00:22,058
By the end,

15
00:00:22,058 --> 00:00:23,579
one US dollar was worth over

16
00:00:23,579 --> 00:00:25,167
four trillion marks.

17
00:00:25,250 --> 00:00:27,131
Money doesn't fail overnight.

18
00:00:27,131 --> 00:00:28,873
It fails when people stop believing

19
00:00:28,873 --> 00:00:29,753
in it.

